{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1551975-exalted-2e-damage-in-spirit-shape-and-false-forms","id":1551975,"title":"Exalted 2e Damage in Spirit Shape and False Forms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-01T11:01:49-07:00","id":1551975,"title":"Exalted 2e Damage in Spirit Shape and False Forms","content":"In a normal combat, the attack roll is Dexterity + Relevant Ability + Relevant Specialty + Accuracy (if any), and the raw damage of the attack is Strength + Weapon Damage (if any) + Extra Successes. In our game the question has come up if the Atk (S/A/D/R) block of a beast Stat Block should be treated as a weapon like a daiklave, or whether the Strength damage is &quot;baked in&quot; to the rating and you no longer add your Strength.<br /> <br /> For me this seems completely wrong. The Atk (S/A/D/R) block is written just like the weapon stat block, and it seems obvious that you add your Strength as normal. I feel that natural weapons are just that, natural WEAPONS. If the Strength damage is &quot;baked in&quot; to the damage of the Atk (S/A/D/R) block, a Tyrant Lizard would have a Bite raw damage of 14L + Extra Successes instead of the 14 Strength + 14L + extra successes I understand it enjoys.<br /> <br /> So my question is &quot;Do animal stat blocks work for raw damage like other damage rolls in the game, being Strength + (Natural) Weapon Damage + Extra successes or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3814,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3814-g3taso","user":"g3taso","date":". 07-01-2025, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3814-g3taso","name":"g3taso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3814_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-01T14:25:49-07:00","id":1551980,"title":"","content":"The stat block should show base damage for the beast in question. As in, what you add attack successes to in able to figure raw damage. Strength is already figured in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-01T16:38:34-07:00","id":1551982,"title":"","content":"I had it wrong! Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3814-g3taso","name":"g3taso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3814_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}